Agentic AI POC – Complete Scope Document
1. Purpose & Core Objective of the POC

The Agentic AI Proof of Concept (POC) is designed to demonstrate end-to-end AI-driven IT automation using Azure AI Foundry, Azure Automation, Hybrid Runbook Worker, SCCM, and supporting enterprise systems.
The POC validates:

Automation feasibility

AI-based runbook selection

Architectural design

Integration touchpoints

Reliability of cloning, publishing, and executing runbooks

Telemetry and diagnostics pipeline

The goal is to automate diagnosing an issue, selecting a corresponding runbook, cloning and publishing it, and executing it on a Hybrid Worker—fully orchestrated by Agentic AI reasoning.

2. High-Level Workflow

A caller (Service Desk, application, or virtual agent) submits an IT issue to an HTTP-triggered Azure Function.

The Azure Function validates incoming payloads, loads configuration from Akeyless, and sends the issue description to an Azure AI Foundry diagnostic agent.

The agent classifies the issue and determines the correct Azure Automation Runbook.

The system fetches the source runbook, clones it, embeds metadata (e.g., machine name, session ID, username), publishes it, and prepares the job for execution.

The cloned runbook is executed on a Hybrid Runbook Worker Group (SCCM-based execution path).

All reasoning steps, decisions, timings, and job metadata are logged to Event Hub.

Integration with systems such as SCCM, ServiceNow, WebMethods APIM, DataPower, and Azure Arc is validated at a connectivity level but not automated in this POC.

3. Functional Scope (In Scope)
3.1 Azure Function

Receives issue descriptions from callers.

Validates payload fields using Pydantic models.

Loads configuration using Akeyless secure vault.

Uses Managed Identity for interacting with Azure services.

Sends validated issue descriptions to Azure AI Foundry diagnostic agents.

3.2 Azure AI Foundry Diagnostic Pipeline

Integration with Azure AI Foundry troubleshooting and diagnostic agents.

AI-based issue classification and runbook mapping.

Logging of all AI reasoning steps and decisions.

3.3 Runbook Cloning & Metadata Injection

Fetching an existing source runbook from Azure Automation.

Cloning the runbook and injecting metadata (machine name, session ID, username, context).

Uploading the cloned runbook.

Publishing the runbook in Azure Automation.

3.4 Runbook Execution

Executing the published runbook via Hybrid Runbook Worker Group (leveraging SCCM path).

Creating and monitoring runbook jobs.

Logging job details, status, and timing.

3.5 Logging & Event Telemetry

Emitting telemetry to Event Hub for each step of the automation pipeline.

Capturing execution timing, diagnostic data, and agentic reasoning context.

3.6 Akeyless Secret Management

Secure retrieval of sensitive configuration values.

Supports both Azure Automation and AI Foundry integration scenarios.

3.7 Integration Layer Validation

Connectivity validation of touchpoints with:

WebMethods

DataPower

ServiceNow

SCCM

Azure Arc

Event Hub

No automated workflows executed against these systems during the POC.

4. Technical Scope

The POC includes the following technologies and components:

Azure Automation Accounts

Hybrid Runbook Worker (HRW) architecture

Azure Event Hub

Azure AI Foundry (diagnostic and decision-making agents)

Managed Identities

Akeyless Secret Manager

Python Azure Function

Pydantic validation models

PowerShell manipulation within cloned runbooks

SCCM-based execution path (trigger only)

Telemetry and instrumentation pipeline

5. Out-of-Scope Items

The following are intentionally excluded from the POC but may be included in future phases:

Production-grade security hardening and compliance controls

Full ServiceNow workflow integration

SCCM remediation workflows beyond runbook execution

Complex conversational multi-step AI agents

Governance, guardrails, SDLC, and enterprise deployment processes

Production release pipelines

Splunk dashboards or Event Hub consumer analytics

Chatbot UI experiences (Teams/Portal)

End-to-end remediation lifecycle beyond runbook invocation

6. POC Deliverables

The POC will produce the following:

Fully functional Azure Function with validation, telemetry, and AI integration

Operational Agentic AI Runbook Resolver

Automated runbook cloning, metadata injection, publishing, and execution workflow

Event Hub logging architecture & implementation

AI diagnostic pipeline with recorded reasoning steps

Architecture diagram (logical and detailed)

Full Python Function codebase

Complete POC scope and technical documentation
